The open source is provided deliberately: everything in this plugin that touches
your machine, your files, and the network is auditable Python. See doc/NETWORK.md
for exactly what the engine sends over the network and how to verify it yourself.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. ENGINE BINARIES  (proprietary — separate EULA)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The compiled QuantFunc inference engine distributed with, or downloaded by, this
plugin is PROPRIETARY and closed-source. This includes (non-exhaustively):

    bin/linux/libquantfunc.so      bin/linux/libquantfunc-12.so
    bin/windows/quantfunc.dll      (and the corresponding CLI executables)

These binaries are NOT covered by the open-source terms in section 1. They are
licensed separately under the QuantFunc End User License Agreement (EULA), and
their use requires a valid QuantFunc license key (api_key). You may not
reverse-engineer, decompile, disassemble, or redistribute the engine binaries
except to the extent expressly permitted by the EULA or by applicable law.

